(3. Market, revenue, competition) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(- Target user is a hypothesis: a small cross-border seller who sources from factories and negotiates in chat.) Tj
T*
(- HMRC 2025: 334,294 UK goods importers. SAM proxy 132,484 to 239,616 \(formula in docs/MARKET_ANALYSIS.md\).) Tj
T*
(- UK goods from China, 2025: GBP 69.7 billion \(ONS/DBT\). Includes precious metals and large corporates.) Tj
T*
(- Savings-pool ceiling GBP 1.05 billion to GBP 2.09 billion. Large-buyer 1.5 to 3 percent band. Not a TradeFlow result.) Tj
T*
(- Umbrellas \(HS 6601\) are the demo wedge. Other codes use the Comtrade preview script. Customs unit value is reference only and does not set the) Tj
T*
(price.) Tj
T*
(- Revenue model, proposed and not earned: a desk subscription, or a share of savings versus the first-round best quote. No revenue is claimed.) Tj
T*
(- Public prices: Accio, and Alibaba RFQ free for buyers. Pactum, Keelvar, Fairmarkit, Jaggaer, Zycus, Globality are quote-based.) Tj
T*
ET
endstream
endobj
